        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(commands): bound reset-hook transcript reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`loadBeforeResetTranscript` in `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.ts` reads session transcript JSONL files with unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` calls. A runaway or corrupted transcript file could force the `before_reset` hook path to buffer the entire file into memory, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReset-hook transcripts are line-oriented JSONL files. A 16 MiB cap is generous headroom for long sessions while preventing the reset hook path from being used as a memory exhaustion vector. When the cap is exceeded, the hook fires with empty messages, matching the existing fallback behavior for unreadable files.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`before_reset` hooks now safely skip oversized transcripts instead of risking process OOM.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test that writes a transcript exceeding the 16 MiB cap, mocks a `before_reset` hook runner, and asserts the hook fires with empty messages.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/commands-reset-hooks.test.ts --run` passes (13/13 tests).\n\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI ran a standalone Node script that imports the same bounded reader used by the reset-hook path (`readRegularFile` from `src/infra/regular-file.ts`) with the same 16 MiB cap. It exercises both a normal transcript and an oversized transcript:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101479.mjs\nPR #101479 real behavior proof: reset-hook transcript bounded read\nMax bytes: 16777216\nNormal file size: 122\nOversized file size: 16777217\n\n--- Normal transcript ---\nResult: loaded 2 message(s)\nMessages: [{\"role\":\"user\",\"text\":\"hello\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"text\":\"hi\"}]\n\n--- Oversized transcript ---\nResult: rejected before parsing, hook would fire with empty messages\n```\n\nThe normal transcript loads and parses into messages as expected. The oversized transcript (16 MiB + 1 byte) is rejected by `readRegularFile` before any JSONL parsing or downstream hook processing, so `loadBeforeResetTranscript` returns empty messages and the `before_reset` hook fires safely without buffering the runaway file.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-reset-hook-transcript-read",
